<title>UK: Bad weather keeps Novorossiisk oil port closed.</title>
<headline>Bad weather keeps Novorossiisk oil port closed.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Black Sea port of Novorossiisk, Russia's leading oil export terminal, remained shut on Tuesday after closing on Monday because of high winds and swell, a reliable shipping source said.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk closed at midday local time on Monday following 24 hours of uninterrupted loading, the source said.</p>
<p>Bad weather has kept the port closed for much of February, leading to loading delays of about five days, traders said.</p>
<p>Five crude tankers were at anchor outside the port on Tuesday, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>Other Black Sea oil ports at Odessa and Tuapse were operating normally, as was Latvia's Ventspils terminal on the Baltic, the source said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
</text>
